# /category-research

This skill takes a {{pipeline.stageA.inputNoun|| "category name"}} from
{{org.approverTitle}} and researches the space, returning a structured
breakdown that defines exactly what kind of {{vocabulary.entity}} the team
is looking for — so that when the search runs, it's pointed at the right
target from the start.

---

## Before anything — reuse check (Rule O4)

Load `standards/OUTPUT-STANDARDS.md` and apply Rule O4 in full before any
research, any API call, or any other step in this file. Reuse is never
silent: say in the visible output which prior run was reused, its date,
and the split between carried-forward and new.

The unit here is the {{pipeline.stageA.unitNoun|| "category"}}. One this
skill has already researched and {{org.approverTitle}} has already
approved is not researched again — compare against the most recent
approved brief for this {{pipeline.stageA.unitNoun|| "category"}} slug
before writing anything. A genuinely different one, or a scope change the
person names, is new work; the same one a day later is not.
